Do not wait 60 s for a firmware helper that does not exist.

The AS21xxx PHY asks for its firmware during the MDIO scan, which runs several
seconds before the root filesystem is mounted, so the direct load fails with
-ENOENT. CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK then makes the kernel wait for a
userspace helper OpenWrt does not ship -- 60 seconds of nothing, and because the
request is synchronous it delays the whole boot: root was mounted at 74 s
instead of 16 s.

Scoped to this board: prepare.sh applies patches/<board>/ only for the board
being built, so the five other filogic boards keep the generic default.

--- a/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
@@ -180,6 +180,7 @@
 CONFIG_FWNODE_MDIO=y
 CONFIG_FW_LOADER_PAGED_BUF=y
 CONFIG_FW_LOADER_SYSFS=y
+# CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK is not set
 CONFIG_GCC_SUPPORTS_DYNAMIC_FTRACE_WITH_ARGS=y
 CONFIG_GENERIC_ALLOCATOR=y
 CONFIG_GENERIC_ARCH_TOPOLOGY=y
